# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/target/

# Cargo lock files — keep the workspace lockfile, ignore sub-crate ones
# (workspace root Cargo.lock is kept)
!Cargo.lock

# IDE / editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Noctivue compiler artifacts (future)
*.nvir
*.nvc

# In-tree Noctivue build outputs. Per docs/TOOLCHAIN.md §3, `.noct/`
# holds ONLY build outputs — fetched dependency content graduates to
# the global content-addressed store, and the committed offline escape
# hatch is `vendor/` (deliberately NOT ignored).
.noct/
# ...except the module-graph fixture that simulates a fetched cache
# tree so vendor-vs-cache precedence stays tested.
!tests/fixtures/modules/.noct/

# Local SQLite files (reference app + scratch databases create these
# at runtime; the checked-in arteries never include live data)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# Native toolchain outputs — never commit binaries (removed a batch of
# accidentally-pushed debug_*.exe/.pdb in the past; this rule exists so
# it cannot recur). Scratch single-file debug scripts (debug_*.rs) and
# captured logs (*_output.txt) belong outside the repo too.
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.obj
debug_*.rs
*_output.txt
